.TH DXDFIR 1 "2026-09-17" "dxdfir 0.6.0" "DX_DFIR Manual"
.SH NAME
dxdfir \- DX_DFIR forensic processing pipeline front-end
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dxdfir
.RI [ --version ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS ...]
.br
.B dxdfir process
.RI [ COLLECTION ]
.RI [ LANE ]
.RB [ --force ]
.RB [ --repo-root
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ --extra-var
.IR KEY=VALUE ]...
.br
.B dxdfir build-car
.RI [ PROCESSED_DIR ]
.RB [ --in
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ --out
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ --rebuild ]
.br
.B dxdfir verify-car
.RB [ --car-dir
.IR DIR ]
.br
.B dxdfir build-timeline
.I CAR_DIR
.RB [ --out
.IR PATH ]
.br
.B dxdfir validate
.br
.B dxdfir verify-images
.br
.B dxdfir build-docker
.RB [ --image
.IR NAME ]...
.RB [ --force ]
.RB [ --repo-root
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ --extra-var
.IR KEY=VALUE ]...
.br
.B dxdfir list
.RB [ lanes | raw | processed | collections ]
.br
.B dxdfir register
.RB [ collection ]
.RI [ NAME ]
.RB [ --from
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ --no-hash ]
.br
.B dxdfir unregister
.RB [ collection ]
.I NAME
.br
.B dxdfir select
.RB [ collection ]
.I NAME
.br
.B dxdfir unselect
.RB [ collection ]
.br
.B dxdfir sort
.RB [ collection ]
.RI [ NAME ]
.RB [ --dry-run ]
.RB [ --no-register ]
.RB [ --no-hash ]
.br
.BR "dxdfir deploy" | destroy | start | stop | status " " stack
.br
.B dxdfir cleanup
.BR processed | car | docker
.RB [ --dry-run ]
.RB [ -y ]
.br
.B dxdfir stix
.I SUBCOMMAND
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dxdfir
is the user-facing front-end of the DX_DFIR pipeline \(em an offline,
container-based digital-forensics workflow that turns raw evidence (packet
captures, disk images, memory, Windows event logs) into normalised JSON,
materialised MITRE CAR and detection events for the Elastic-native analysis
backend.
.PP
It is the top of a three-layer design: this command holds the verbs, the
.B get_sybers.dxdfir
Ansible collection holds the orchestration (one role per source, one action per
task), and the
.B get_sybers_dxdfir
Python package holds the heavy per-item processing the roles invoke.
.PP
.B dxdfir process
drives a source's role with
.BR ansible-playbook (1)
\(em preflight, then process, then verify \(em and the role's single action calls
.RB \(lq python \-m get_sybers_dxdfir. SOURCE \(rq
for the tight loop.
.BR build-car ", " verify-car " and " build-timeline
drive the CAR lane the same way (the
.B dxdfir_byakugan
role over the external Byakugan engine, run inside the hardened
.B get-sybers/byakugan
image \(em cloned + built at the
.I sources.yml
pin by
.BR "dxdfir build-docker" ,
so the lane only shells the image \(em and the
.B get_sybers_dxdfir.carcheck
gate), while
.B validate
fronts the repository's check harness
.RB ( .github/tests/run-checks.sh ).
The analysis backend itself (the Elastic stack under
.IR docker/elastic )
is brought up with
.B deploy stack
(the
.B dxdfir_stack
role) or docker compose; see its README.
.SH COMMANDS
Commands read verb first \(em \fBregister collection\fR \fINAME\fR,
\fBdeploy stack\fR, \fBlist collections\fR. The collection verbs also take a
bare \fINAME\fR in place of the noun: \fBregister\fR \fINAME\fR is
\fBregister collection\fR \fINAME\fR. The former noun-first spellings
(\fBcollection register\fR, \fBstack deploy\fR) still run, hidden, and print
the verb-first form to use.
.TP
.BI "process " [COLLECTION] " " [LANE]
Process evidence with a lane. \fILANE\fR is one of
.BR zeek ", " evtx ", " memory ", " plaso ", " godfir-toolz ", " signatures ", " all
(the default when a collection is given); \fICOLLECTION\fR scopes the run to one
registered collection (else the active one, if set). The two positionals may be
given in either order \(em a lane name is the lane, anything else the collection.
Idempotent: inputs that already have output are skipped (use
.B --force
to reprocess).
.TP
.BI "build-car " [PROCESSED_DIR]
Build the per-source CAR stores (car.db + superset.db + one
.IR car_<object>.jsonl
per object) from the processed tree \(em every source under it by default, or
one file/dir with
.BR --in .
A source whose store already exists is left alone unless
.B --rebuild
is given.
.TP
.B verify-car
The CAR correctness gate over the materialised CAR
.RI ( data_store/processed/byakugan
by default, or
.BR --car-dir ):
each exercised object populated, values sane (IPs, ports, SIDs,
.I car_action
in the engine model's vocabulary), every row traceable to one artefact, the
relationship edges naming real endpoints. Run the pipeline first
(process, then build-car).
.TP
.BI "build-timeline " CAR_DIR
Build one property-rich, time-ordered CAR timeline JSONL from a source's
car.db + superset.db (or aggregate a whole tree). Alias:
.BR car-timeline .
.TP
.B validate
Run the repository check harness (fronts
.IR .github/tests/run-checks.sh ).
.TP
.B verify-images
Audit the hardened
.I get-sybers/*
tool-image inventory: every expected image present and hardened, nothing
unexpected in the namespace.
.TP
.B build-docker
Build (and hardening-verify) the
.I get-sybers/*
tool images from the in-repo Dockerfiles. Fronts
.I playbooks/dxdfir-build-images.yml
(the
.B dxdfir_images
role): each image is built from its ansible-hardened Dockerfile under
.IR docker/ ,
then the hardening contract is asserted on the result (fixed non-root
.BR USER ,
.B com.get-sybers.hardened
label, no
.BR apt-get / dpkg / sudo / pip /ansible;
shell + python absent from the tool-only images). Restrict the set with
.B --image
(repeatable); rebuild existing images with
.BR --force .
Run once per host before first processing, and again after changing anything
under
.IR docker/ .
.TP
.BI "list " [VIEW]
Inventory the staged evidence, or the collections. \fIVIEW\fR is
.B lanes
(the default: for each lane that
.B process
reads, the input directory and how many evidence files are present),
.B raw
or
.B processed
(a directory view of that tree's top-level subdirs), or
.B collections
(registered, detected and dropzone-candidate collections; the active one is
starred).
.TP
.BI "register [collection] " [NAME]
Register a collection: promote \fIdata_store/raw/sort/NAME/\fR if it exists
(loose files auto-classified into lane subdirs), else create an empty
collection \(em or, with
.BI --from " PATH" ,
symlink an external directory in (\fINAME\fR defaults to its basename). Adds
the SQLite registry row and SHA-1s the evidence into
.I .collection.hashes
unless
.BR --no-hash .
.TP
.BI "unregister [collection] " NAME
Drop the registry row and marker; evidence and log are preserved.
.TP
.BI "select [collection] " NAME
Mark a collection as the active target for later commands
.RB ( process ", " sort ).
.TP
.B unselect [collection]
Clear the active collection.
.TP
.BI "sort [collection] " [NAME]
Sort the dropzone into the collection's lanes by magic-byte type (content beats
extension). With no \fINAME\fR the active collection is used, or the only one.
.B --dry-run
shows what would move.
.TP
.BR "deploy stack" ", " "destroy stack" ", " "start stack" ", " "stop stack" ", " "status stack"
The analysis-stack lifecycle (the
.B dxdfir_stack
role over
.IR docker/elastic ):
build if needed and bring the stack up, then verify it; stop and remove its
containers and networks
.RB ( --volumes
also wipes the named volumes, i.e. the ingested data); start the existing
stopped containers; stop them but keep them; show their status. The noun is
required \(em a bare verb lists its targets.
.TP
\fBcleanup processed\fR|\fBcar\fR|\fBdocker\fR
Wipe
.I data_store/processed/
(every lane and the CAR), the materialised CAR tree only, or the built
.I get-sybers/*
tool images (the
.B dxdfir_cleanup
role). Each prompts unless
.B -y
is given;
.B --dry-run
maps to
.BR "ansible-playbook --check" .
.TP
.BI "stix " SUBCOMMAND
The STIX 2.1 / OpenCTI exchange verbs (detections to sightings, indicators in,
sightings back); see
.BR "dxdfir stix -h" .
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Global
.TP
.B --version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR --help ", " -h
Show help and exit. Accepted at every level, e.g.\&
.BR "dxdfir -h" " or " "dxdfir " \fICOMMAND\fR " -h" .
Each level shows its own options.
.SS process
.TP
.B --force
Reprocess inputs that already have output.
.TP
.BI --repo-root " PATH"
DX_DFIR repository root. Auto-detected otherwise (see
.BR ENVIRONMENT ).
.TP
.BR --extra-var ", " -e " " \fIKEY=VALUE\fR
Pass an extra Ansible variable through to the role; repeatable. Use it to override
a role default, e.g.
.RB \(lq -e\  dxdfir_zeek_pcap_dir=/evidence/pcaps \(rq
or
.RB \(lq -e\  \(aq{\(dqdxdfir_signatures_lanes\(dq:[\(dqyara\(dq]}\(aq \(rq.
.SS register
.TP
.BR --from ", " -f " " \fIPATH\fR
Source: a dropzone subfolder or an external directory to symlink in.
.TP
.B --no-hash
Skip SHA-1 hashing the evidence into
.IR .collection.hashes .
.SS sort
.TP
.B --dry-run
Show what would move; move nothing.
.TP
.B --no-register
Sort an unregistered collection without registering it.
.TP
.B --no-hash
Skip the hash-manifest refresh after sorting.
.SS build-car
.TP
.BI --in " PATH"
Single-source mode: one processed file or directory, one car.db.
.TP
.BI --out " DIR"
Output directory (single-source: this source's car dir; batch: the car/ root).
.TP
.BI --host " HOST"
Single-source mode: fallback source_host where the map derives none.
.TP
.B --rebuild
Rebuild CAR stores that already exist (after a map/coverage change).
.SS verify-car
.TP
.BI --car-dir " DIR"
The materialised CAR tree to check. Default:
.IR <repo>/data_store/processed/byakugan .
.SS build-docker
.TP
.BR --image ", " -i " " \fINAME\fR
Build only this image (e.g.\&
.BR yara ,
.BR zeek ,
.BR anamnesis );
repeatable. Default: every get-sybers/* tool image.
.TP
.B --force
Rebuild even when the image already exists (docker layer cache still applies).
.TP
.BI --repo-root " PATH"
DX_DFIR repository root. Auto-detected otherwise (see
.BR ENVIRONMENT ).
.TP
.BR --extra-var ", " -e " " \fIKEY=VALUE\fR
Pass an extra Ansible variable through to the
.B dxdfir_images
role; repeatable (e.g.\&
.RB \(lq -e\  dxdfir_runtime_uid=3000 \(rq).
.SS deploy stack
.TP
.B --no-build
Do not build images before starting.
.SS destroy stack
.TP
.B --volumes
Also remove the named volumes (wipes the ingested data).
.TP
.BR --yes ", " -y
Do not prompt.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DFIR_REPO_ROOT
Repository root, used when
.B --repo-root
is not given. If neither is set, the repo is found by walking up from the current
directory, then from the dxdfir binary's own location.
.TP
.B ANSIBLE_ROLES_PATH
Set by every verb that drives
.BR ansible-playbook (1)
to the collection's roles directory so the roles resolve without installing the
collection.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B dxdfir
exits
.B 0
on success and propagates the exit status of the underlying
.BR ansible-playbook (1)
run or tool on failure;
.B 1
for a usage error (an unknown verb, flag or argument count);
.B 2
for a lookup error (e.g. the repo or a playbook could not be found, or no
materialised CAR to verify) and
.B 127
if a required tool is not on
.BR PATH .
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Build every hardened tool image (first-run setup, or after touching docker/):
.B dxdfir build-docker
.TP
Rebuild just the YARA image:
.B dxdfir build-docker --image yara --force
.TP
Process packet captures with the zeek lane:
.B dxdfir process zeek
.TP
Reprocess memory images, overriding the input directory:
.B dxdfir process memory --force -e dxdfir_memory_memory_dir=/evidence/mem
.TP
Run only the YARA signature lane:
.B dxdfir process signatures -e \(aq{\(dqdxdfir_signatures_lanes\(dq:[\(dqyara\(dq]}\(aq
.TP
Register the dropzone folder data_store/raw/sort/case-a as a tracked collection, sort it, make it active, process it:
.B dxdfir register case-a && dxdfir sort case-a && dxdfir select case-a && dxdfir process case-a
.TP
Bring the analysis stack up, then show what is running:
.B dxdfir deploy stack && dxdfir status stack
.TP
Normalise everything processed into CAR, then gate it:
.B dxdfir build-car && dxdfir verify-car
.TP
One timeline across every source:
.B dxdfir build-timeline data_store/processed/byakugan --out /tmp/timeline.jsonl
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ansible/collections/get_sybers.dxdfir/
The Ansible collection driven by
.BR "dxdfir process" .
.TP
.I python/get_sybers_dxdfir/
The processing package (also runnable as
.RB \(lq python\ -m\ get_sybers_dxdfir. SOURCE \(rq).
.TP
.I data_store/
Raw evidence and processed output (gitignored); the materialised CAR lands under
.IR data_store/processed/byakugan/ .
.TP
.I docker/elastic/
The Elastic-native analysis backend (docker compose).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ansible-playbook (1),
.BR docker (1).
The processors run standalone as
.RB \(lq python\ -m\ get_sybers_dxdfir. SOURCE \ --help\(rq.
